  "decision_note_2026_08_03": "86 of 1503 days have a short leg that rounds to zero whole shares (SPY/IVV priced in the hundreds against a ~$500 per-leg allocation at this account size) while the long leg fills normally - on those days this isn't a market-neutral pairs trade, it's one-legged directional exposure the strategy never intended. The prior 'reject' verdict (a 0.017 Sharpe difference on a sleeve averaging 2.47% gross and 0.23% vol) was measuring that distortion as much as the hypothesis. performance_fractional_diagnostic shows what a symmetric-fractional version would look like, but Alpaca cannot actually short ETFs fractionally, so that variant is not something this account could deploy - it is included only to show whether the whole-share floor is masking a real signal, not as a promotable alternative. The original gate's reject/promote verdict is preserved below for continuity, but decision reflects that the tested strategy was not the pre-registered one on a meaningful fraction of days.",
